# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: Other | Scene: MarionOrVargaPath

translate es strings:

    old "It was more than two weeks after the victory over the eastern tribesmen, when Sarah arrived early for a council meeting, surprised to find the room already full."
    new "Habían pasado más de dos semanas desde la victoria sobre los miembros de las tribus orientales cuando Sarah llegó temprano a una reunión del consejo, sorprendida al encontrar la sala ya llena."

    old "There was a busy chatter, which suddenly felt silent as everyone noticed Sarah."
    new "Había un bullicio animado, que de repente quedó en silencio cuando todos se fijaron en Sarah."

    old "Thomas was sitting back in this throne, waiving at Sarah excitedly as she approached."
    new "Thomas estaba reclinado en el trono, saludando emocionadamente a Sarah mientras ella se acercaba."

    old "Sarah had almost reached the table, when suddenly, Marion stood up."
    new "Sarah casi había llegado a la mesa cuando, de repente, Marion se levantó."

    old "Sarah saw Thomas suppress laughter. In between his laughs he managed to speak."
    new "Sarah vio cómo Tomás reprimía la risa. Entre una risa y otra, logró hablar."

    old "I believe our honorable friend, Marion, has something he wanted to say to you."
    new "Creo que nuestro honorable amigo, Marion, tiene algo que quiere decirte."

    old "Sarah could feel a pit in her stomach."
    new "Sarah podía sentir un nudo en el estómago."

    old "She feared she already knew what he was planning to do."
    new "Temía saber ya lo que él planeaba hacer."

    old "Confused, Sarah stared at Marion."
    new "Confundida, Sarah miró fijamente a Marion."

    old "Marion fell to one knee, and extended a hand, holding a small box carved out of oak."
    new "Marion se arrodilló sobre una rodilla y le extendió una mano, sosteniendo una pequeña caja tallada en roble."

    old "Sarah Rose, having given it serious consideration, I wish to pronounce in front of all these people, my love for you."
    new "Sarah Rose, después de haberlo considerado seriamente, deseo declarar ante toda esta gente mi amor por ti."

    old "Please give me the honour of your hand, and I will swear to always be true."
    new "Por favor, concédeme el honor de tu mano, y te juro que siempre seré fiel."

    old "Stunned, Sarah felt it almost physically difficult to remain standing."
    new "Atónita, Sarah sintió que le resultaba casi físicamente difícil permanecer de pie."

    old "The edges of her vision seemed to blur, and the ground under her feet began to shift."
    new "Los bordes de su visión parecieron difuminarse, y el suelo bajo sus pies comenzó a desplazarse."

    old "Accept Marion's proposal."
    new "Aceptar la propuesta de Marion."

    old "Yes."
    new "Sí."

    old "The words seemed to slip out before she had given it any thought."
    new "Las palabras parecieron escapársele antes de que pudiera pensarlas."

    old "She saw the faces around the table, clearly, she was not alone in her surprised."
    new "Vio los rostros alrededor de la mesa; claramente, no era la única sorprendida."

    old "Still on his knees, she saw Marion's face beaming."
    new "Aún de rodillas, vio el rostro de Marion, radiante."

    old "She watched as he rose to his feet, grabbed her by the waist and spun her around."
    new "Ella observó cómo él se levantaba, la agarraba por la cintura y la hacía girar."

    old "All around the room, people began to give their congratulations to the new couple."
    new "Por toda la sala, la gente empezó a felicitar a la nueva pareja."

    old "Varga was the only one who carried a pained expression on his face."
    new "Varga era el único que tenía una expresión de dolor en el rostro."

    old "Sarah watched it all unfold as if this was happening to someone else."
    new "Sarah observaba cómo todo sucedía como si le estuviera ocurriendo a otra persona."

    old "Reject Marion's proposal."
    new "Rechazar la propuesta de Marion."

    old "Suddenly, Sarah felt all the emotions of the shock pushed out and she found her footing again."
    new "De repente, Sarah sintió cómo todas las emociones del shock eran expulsadas de ella, y logró recuperar el equilibrio."

    old "Rage was now keeping her tethered."
    new "La rabia era ahora lo que la mantenía atada."

    old "In only two broad steps she closed the distance between herself and Marion, standing over the imbecile as he was still kneeling."
    new "En apenas dos amplios pasos, cerró la distancia que la separaba de Marion, plantándose sobre el imbécil mientras él seguía arrodillado."

    old "A more humble man would have seen the signs of what came next, but Marion was not humble."
    new "Un hombre más humilde habría visto las señales de lo que vendría después, pero Marion no era humilde."

    old "A shattering crack rang out across the room, followed by a deafening silence."
    new "Un crujido estremecedor resonó por toda la habitación, seguido de un silencio ensordecedor."

    old "Marion's face was frozen off to the side, unable to process the slap, either physically or emotionally."
    new "El rostro de Marion estaba congelado hacia un lado, incapaz de procesar la bofetada, ni física ni emocionalmente."

    old "Sarah could see from the corners of her eyes that everyone was staring at her."
    new "Sarah podía ver por el rabillo del ojo que todos la miraban fijamente."

    old "Marriage?"
    new "¿Matrimonio?"

    old "Are you insane?"
    new "¿Estás loca?"

    old "We were nothing more than friends at best, Marion."
    new "En el mejor de los casos, no éramos más que amigos, Marion."

    old "I never gave you my blessing, I never agreed to any of this."
    new "Nunca te di mi bendición, nunca estuve de acuerdo con nada de esto."

    old "And if you thought I would feel forced to say yes because we were in public, you're as big of an idiot as you are craven."
    new "Y si creías que me sentiría obligada a decir que sí porque estábamos en público, eres tan idiota como cobarde."

    old "The only thing you've managed to do today is humiliate me, and make a joke of yourself."
    new "Lo único que has logrado hacer hoy es humillarme y convertirte en el hazmerreír de todos."

    old "Marion was now crawling away from her, trying to recover and get back on his feet."
    new "Marion ahora se arrastraba lejos de ella, intentando recuperarse y volver a ponerse de pie."

    old "By the time he had gotten onto his feet, Sarah could see his face had turned bright red."
    new "Para cuando él logró ponerse de pie, Sarah ya podía ver que su rostro se había puesto completamente rojo."

    old "I brought it up with Thomas...he thought it would be..."
    new "Se lo mencioné a Thomas... él pensó que sería..."

    old "A joke, Marion. He probably thought you were a joke, and I suppose, in that regard, he was right."
    new "Es una broma, Marion. Probablemente pensó que eras una broma, y supongo que, en ese sentido, tenía razón."

    old "I don't want to see you here ever again. You're off the council."
    new "No quiero volver a verte aquí nunca más. Estás fuera del consejo."

    old "Leave, and pray that nobody ever hears how much you humiliated yourself today."
    new "Vete, y reza para que nadie se entere de lo mucho que te has humillado hoy."

    old "Marion searched for words, but unable to find any, turned around and stormed off."
    new "Marion buscó las palabras adecuadas, pero, incapaz de encontrarlas, se dio la vuelta y se marchó furioso."

    old "Sarah snapped back to the table full of advisors."
    new "Sarah volvió bruscamente a la mesa llena de consejeros."

    old "Her eyes ran across all the faces. Most were a mix of stunned and mortified, there was only one exception."
    new "Sus ojos recorrieron todos los rostros. La mayoría mostraba una mezcla de asombro y vergüenza; solo había una excepción."

    old "Varga was brightly smiling, clearly having enjoyed the humiliation of Marion."
    new "Varga sonreía radiante, claramente habiendo disfrutado de la humillación de Marion."

    old "If I find out any of you set him up to this, I swear you're going to pay for it."
    new "Si descubro que alguno de vosotros le tendió una trampa para que llegara a esto, juro que vais a pagar por ello."

    old "Sarah herself now turned around and stormed off, in no mood to continue the council meeting."
    new "La propia Sarah se dio la vuelta y se marchó furiosa, sin ánimo alguno de continuar la reunión del consejo."
